    "description": "**Pick this tool for backup INVENTORY and backup HISTORY questions.**\n\nThis tool lists backups available in the configured Catalyst Center backup storage with optional filtering, sorting, and pagination. It returns backup identifiers plus summary fields such as status, dates, size, scope, storage, compatibility, and availability.\n\n**Use this tool when the user asks:**\n- to show all backups or available backups\n- whether there are failed backups\n- which backups are available for restore\n- for backup history or recent backups\n- for backups created by a specific user, status, or time period\n- for a list of backups before drilling into one backup in detail\n\n**Pick this tool for questions like:**\n- \"Show me all backups\"\n- \"List available backups\"\n- \"Are there any failed backups?\"\n- \"What backups can be restored?\"\n- \"Show the latest backups\"\n- \"Show backups created by system\"\n- \"List backups from the last week\"\n\n**Do NOT use this tool for:**\n- current backup configuration/settings\n- mounted backup storage capacity questions\n- configured NFS server health\n- detailed diagnostics for one backup execution\n\nWhen the user wants full package, version, or compatibility details for a single backup, first call this tool to get the backup `id`, then call `api_getBackupById`.",
    "name": "api_getAllBackup",
    "parameters": {
      "properties": {
        "limit": {
          "description": "Optional maximum number of backup records to return. Valid range is 1-500. Use a smaller limit when the user wants a compact page of results.",
          "maximum": 500,
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "offset": {
          "description": "Optional 1-based starting offset for pagination. Use 1 for the first page, then increase it to page through additional or older backups.",
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "order": {
          "description": "Optional sort direction. Use `desc` for newest-first or latest-first views and `asc` for oldest-first or alphabetical order.",
          "enum": [
            "asc",
            "desc"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "query": {
          "description": "Optional free-text filter for backup records, useful for narrowing by backup name, status, creator, scope, or other searchable backup fields.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "sortBy": {
          "description": "Optional backup response field to sort by, such as `createdDate`, `endDate`, `name`, or `status`.",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [],
      "type": "object"
    },
